; A number's six digits, held as two numbers of three digits, out as the digits. Cards pass through but for -15
; and -17 (from numd): after -15 and the count come hi and lo, and out go -15, the count and the six digits, for
; numw; after -17 come hi and lo, the first six digits of a number of seven or more, and out go the six digits as
; word cards, 700 + d. Each digit is the first of hi, which then moves on a digit (lo's first coming in at its end).
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            rec     INP   x        03-21: a card; a number's digits
  04                    CLA   x
  05                    ADD   n16
  06                    TAC   long
  07                    OUT   x
  08                    SUB   00
  09                    SUB   00
  10                    TAC   num
  11                    JMP   rec
  12            num     INP   x
  13                    OUT   x
  14                    CLA   z
  15                    JMP   set
  16            long    CLA   c700
  17            set     STO   base
  18                    INP   hi
  19                    INP   lo
  20                    CLA   n5
  21                    STO   i
  22            each    CLA   hi       22-41: six digits
  23                    SFT   02
  24                    ADD   base
  25                    STO   x
  26                    OUT   x
  27                    CLA   lo
  28                    SFT   02
  29                    STO   t
  30                    CLA   hi
  31                    SFT   10
  32                    ADD   t
  33                    STO   hi
  34                    CLA   lo
  35                    SFT   10
  36                    STO   lo
  37                    CLA   i
  38                    SUB   00
  39                    STO   i
  40                    TAC   rec
  41                    JMP   each
  50            x       DATA  0
  51            hi      DATA  0
  52            lo      DATA  0
  53            t       DATA  0
  54            i       DATA  0
  55            base    DATA  0
  56            z       DATA  0
  57            n16     DATA  16
  58            n5      DATA  5
  59            c700    DATA  700
